      {
        "id": 73051,
        "name": "jagarciao",
        "username": "jagarciao",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-12T00:17:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Most of La Capitan's names are given names and not traditional Spanish family surnames, so I think they might have more to do with the different identities she has had through time than with the traditional long-form Spanish naming conventions.&nbsp;</p><p>The names using \"de\" can reflect secondary names assigned at some point due to land holdings, affiliations, or places of origin... or given to females when they marry (they take their husbands last name after their own preceded by \"de\").&nbsp;</p><p>The long form is traditionally created by going back one generation and adding all the last names in that generation in the order of strongest paternal lineage and then moving back another generation and doing the same, but skipping the names you already used (unless the name is coming from a different line, then you can repeat it).&nbsp;</p><p>For instance, in the attached picture I create a (fictitious) long-form name for myself. The new blue names in each generation go first, then the reds. The order of blues is determined by how strongly they are linked to the blues below them. Kinda confusing, but the picture should help.&nbsp;</p><p>They do increase by order of two in each generation, but it is common to have missing genealogical information and therefore not be able to complete a tier.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/f/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2\" title=\"image_6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2_2_690x131.jpeg\" alt=\"image_6.jpg\" data-base62-sha1=\"zS4rSL28Klaz2esWKQFwHaRjRIK\" width=\"690\" height=\"131\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2_2_690x131.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2_2_1035x196.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/f/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb68d55d74f9c3d38a0ad5a63910be0d0cb174e2_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image_6.jpg</span><span class=\"informations\">1141×217 54.1 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
